# Reading the statusline
`SKILL.md` defines when to enable it and its boundaries. This document explains
**how to interpret the numbers after enabling it**.
## Three display modes
| Mode | Lines | Added information |
|---|---|---|
| `compact` | 1 | Model, context, cost, 5-hour/7-day limits |
| `normal` | 2 | Project, session ID, elapsed time, burn rate, todos |
| `detailed` | 6 | Configuration counts, token breakdown, predictions, other CLI limits |
Choose with `/jstack:dashboard-setup`. Settings go to `~/.claude/claude-dashboard.local.json`.
**The filename remains upstream's**: bundled code reads it, so do not rename it.
## Using it without emoji: measured configuration
Default modes measured with our `block_emoji.py` detector:
| Mode | Distinct emoji |
|---|---|
| `compact` | 1 (U+26A0) |
| `normal` | 2 (U+26A0, U+23F1) |
| `detailed` | 7 |
**A zero-emoji configuration exists.** `disabledWidgets` cannot remove compact's
U+26A0 through that path. Choose widgets with `custom` instead.
```json
{
"displayMode": "custom",
"lines": [["model", "context", "cost", "rateLimit5h", "rateLimit7d", "rateLimit7dFable"],
["sessionName", "version"]]
}
```
Measured result: **zero emoji**, with a real workspace directory in the input,
both with readable rate limits and with none:
```
◆ Opus(H) │ ████░░░░░░ │ 40% │ 80K/200K │ $3.20 │ 5h: 42% (1h59m) │ 7d: 93% (4d15h)
v2.1.0
```
`/jstack:dashboard-setup noemoji` writes this configuration.
**Do not add `projectInfo`.** It prints U+1F4C1 (folder) whenever the input carries
a workspace directory, which every real session does. An earlier measurement
listed it as emoji-free because its sample input had no directory, so the widget
rendered nothing. Measure candidate widgets with a directory present.
**The limit widgets stay emoji-free in both states.** Upstream printed U+26A0 from
`rateLimit5h` when limit data could not be read (logged out, API key, request
failure). A local change in `scripts/widgets/rate-limit.ts` names that state in
text instead, keeping the label: `5h: --`. `rateLimit7d` and `rateLimit7dFable`
hide themselves in the same state, and `7d-F` arrives only from the API, never
from stdin, so it is absent until a usage request succeeds.
`◆`, `█`, and `│` **are not emoji**. Upstream `scripts/utils/emoji.ts` explicitly
excludes non-emoji typographic symbols, and our hook also accepts them. Measurement:
U+25C6, U+2588, and U+2502 passed; U+26A0, U+23F1, and U+2705 were blocked.
For less output, use `{"displayMode":"custom","lines":[["context","cost"]]}`.
This two-widget configuration also emits zero emoji.
## Widgets
The widget table in the `/jstack:dashboard-setup` command is authoritative for all 38
widgets and their meanings. This section covers common or confusing values.
| Widget | Interpretation |
|---|---|
| `context` | Progress bar, percentage, and used tokens/window size; percentage helps anticipate compaction |
| `cost` | Accumulated USD for **this session**; `todayCost` covers the whole day |
| `rateLimit5h`, `rateLimit7d` | Plan allowance consumed; `depletionTime` predicts exhaustion at the current rate |
| `burnRate` | Tokens per minute; spikes indicate large tool-output intervals |
| `cacheHit` | Cache hit rate; low values indicate prompt prefixes changing each turn |
| `codexUsage`, `geminiUsage`, `antigravityUsage`, `zaiUsage` | Shown **only when the corresponding CLI is installed**; absence is not a defect |
| `budget` | Requires `dailyBudget` configuration |
`contextBar`, `contextPercentage`, and `contextUsage` are components of `context`
and can be placed separately.
## Missing output
| Symptom | First check |
|---|---|
| No statusline | Was `/jstack:dashboard-setup` run for this config directory? Absence before setup is normal |
| Set up but absent | Use `/jstack:dashboard-repair`; its `status` step shows the owner, shim, and resolved build |
| Only one CLI's limits are absent | Check CLI installation/login; the widget hides itself when unavailable |
| Warning symbol instead of limits | Limit data could not be read; check login state |
| Old values after updating | Each render resolves the latest version again; use dashboard-repair if the issue persists |
## One-time query
```
/jstack:check-usage # Human-readable
/jstack:check-usage --json # Machine-readable
/jstack:check-usage --lang ko
```
No statusline is required. Use `/jstack:dashboard-alias` for a shell alias.
